jobResponsibilities:
As a TIER officer in the Trade Strategy and Security Division, you will be part of a dynamic team working on fast-moving pieces to help Singapore navigate changes in our geo-economic environment. You will have the opportunity to hone your strategic thinking skillset, policy acumen, and international orientation perspectives in both the economic and security domains, by:

•	Assessing the impact and implications of geo-political developments on Singapore’s economic and security interests;

•	Developing strategies, policies, options and responses to expand Singapore’s economic heft or relevance as well as strengthen Singapore’s economic resilience;

•	Preparing and executing communications and engagement strategies with key public and private sector stakeholders;

•	Organising and representing MTI at various high-level inter-agency platforms related to economic, security, and geo-political portfolios; and

•	Collaborating and networking with various internal and external stakeholders.

jobRequirements:
We are looking for dedicated team players who thrive in a fast-paced environment with:

•	Relevant field of study in International Relations, Political Science, Public Policy, Economics, Business, Finance, Accounting or any related discipline;

•	Keen interest in the geo-political environment, as well as economic and security issues;

•	Experience in policy formulation and data analysis;

•	Excellent analytical, writing, communication, and presentation skills; and

•	Strong project management and stakeholder management skills.

jobDescription:
The Trade and International Economic Relations (TIER) cluster drives the formulation of Singapore's foreign economic policy and advances Singapore's economic interests in the international economic arena.

MTI’s International Trade Division (ITD) is charged with protecting and advancing Singapore’s economic interests by:

* Supporting free trade and open markets;
* Upholding and strengthening the rules-based multilateral trading system as embodied in the World Trade Organisation (WTO);
* Deepening economic integration with like-minded countries through free trade agreements (FTA) and bilateral investment treaties (BIT);
* Driving initiatives in regional economic fora such as the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC); and
* Advancing our companies’ interests abroad rigorously, including by lowering barriers for Singapore exports

jobResponsibilities:
Responsibilities

As an ITD officer, you will be assigned to one of four specialised teams covering trade in goods, digital economy and services, investment, or multilateral trade policy. You will deepen your knowledge, skills and expertise on a myriad of international trade issues and apply them in the following areas:

* Developing and implementing Singapore’s foreign economic policy;
* Representing Singapore in bilateral/multilateral trade and investment negotiations;
* Participating in international meetings and conferences;
* Providing advice to the Singapore Government on trade policy matters;
* Collaborating with external stakeholders, such as Singapore-based companies, business chambers and the general public;
* Ensuring Singapore’s full and timely implementation of international trade obligations; and
* Analysing international developments and their potential implications on Singapore

