jobResponsibilities:
You will be expected to:
• manage cases filed in the General Division of the High Court, Civil Section through analysing, reviewing, monitoring and processing documents in accordance with the applicable legislation, rules, practice directions, standard operating procedures and policies;
• draft case summaries, reports, notices and general correspondence and liaise with lawyers, self-represented persons and other external agencies to facilitate the efficient disposal of cases;
• Compile, organise and maintain accurate up-to-date case information and statistics on caseload and disposal using the operational systems;
• review and streamline existing operational processes to improve quality and productivity to meet the key performance indicators of the Section and the Registry;
• participate as a team member and be involved in projects which affect the operations of the Registry; and
• perform any other tasks as and when assigned.

You will be involved in the following key work areas:
•	Manage business transactions (e.g. fees & charges, receipts, fixed assets, advance/deposit accounts) to ensure accurate and timely financial reporting in compliance with Instructions Manual and regulatory requirements;
•	Review financial proposals from Divisions to ensure proper governance and compliance (e.g. write-offs, fees below Cost Recovery Ratio, revenue waivers);
•	Compile, review and submit statutory returns to MOF, AGD and senior management as Accounting Officer;
•	Coordinate and facilitate fixed asset audits, including implementation of rectification and improvement measures arising from audit findings;
•	Oversee finance shared services provided by VITAL to ensure service quality and compliance;
•	Perform accounts closing activities, oversee preparation of Government Financial Statements, and respond to audit queries;
•	Participate in finance policy, process and systems reviews, including adoption of automation, analytics and AI tools to enhance efficiency;
•	Act as desk head for Statutory Boards, overseeing finance matters (e.g. budget and funding submissions, governance matters, fee revisions) and grant disbursements.

