jobResponsibilities:
Prime Minister’s Office (PMO) Finance Group was formed with a strong One Public Service mindset to provide finance services across PMO agencies under its care, managing the respective agencies’ budgets to ensure financial accountability, fiscal sustainability, and the effective & efficient use of public resources. PMO Finance Group supports officers in meaningful finance work and are empowered to make improvements to processes and workflows, to formulate internal policies and best practices.

You will be an AGD officer forward deployed to PMO Finance Group. Your responsibilities include: 

• Ensuring optimal provision, allocation and management of the agency’s budget to achieve Government and agency’s strategic objectives in a fiscally sustainable and value-for-money manner; 
• Reviewing and formulating of internal finance policies and procedures for efficient and effective financial administration and strong internal controls; 
• Ensuring all budgetary and financial matters are performed in line with all finance regulations and guidelines;
• Supporting the Internal Approving Authority and Tender Boards by reviewing funding proposals and tender board submissions to ensure that projects undertaken are operationally and financially viable

As a senior legal officer in the Civil Department, your primary functions are: 
• Adjudicate Work Injury Compensation (WIC) cases which includes presiding over hearings, preparing notes of evidence and detailed Grounds of Decisions for appeals to the High Court;
• Guide and mentor junior officers; and
• Develop training materials on contemporary legal topics for legal and non-legal officers in the Ministry.
Your other functions and duties may include the following:
• Rendering legal advice on issues under the Ministry’s purview (including employment law, trade unions, industrial relations, workplace safety and health, work injury compensation, foreign manpower and administrative law (including judicial review) and international law); 
• Reviewing, drafting and vetting legislation administered by the Ministry;
• Collaborating with the Ministry’s policy divisions on legal policy projects; and
• Drafting, vetting and rendering advice on contracts, data disclosure agreements and MOUs.

